{"stored_at": 1793591522.590556, "body": {"results": [{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "Q13671", "secondaryAccessions": ["O15010", "Q00427", "Q96CC8"], "uniProtkbId": "RIN1_HUMAN", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "1997-11-01", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-09-02", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "2006-10-17", "entryVersion": 211, "sequenceVersion": 4}, "annotationScore": 5.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Homo sapiens", "commonName": "Human", "taxonId": 9606, "lineage": ["Eukaryota", "Metazoa", "Chordata", "Craniata", "Vertebrata", "Euteleostomi", "Mammalia", "Eutheria", "Euarchontoglires", "Primates", "Haplorrhini", "Catarrhini", "Hominidae", "Homo"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"value": "Ras and Rab interactor 1"}}, "alternativeNames": [{"fullName": {"value": "Ras inhibitor JC99"}}, {"fullName": {"value": "Ras interaction/interference protein 1"}}]}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"value": "RIN1"}}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "15886098"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9144171"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9208849"}], "value": "Ras effector protein, which may serve as an inhibitory modulator of neuronal plasticity in aversive memory formation. Can affect Ras signaling at different levels. First, by competing with RAF1 protein for binding to activated Ras. Second, by enhancing signaling from ABL1 and ABL2, which regulate cytoskeletal remodeling. Third, by activating RAB5A, possibly by functioning as a guanine nucleotide exchange factor (GEF) for RAB5A, by exchanging bound GDP for free GTP, and facilitating Ras-activated receptor endocytosis"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "15886098"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9208849"}], "value": "Interacts with the GTP-bound form of Ras proteins (NRAS, HRAS and KRAS). This interaction prevents the association between RAF1 and Ras. Interacts with 14-3-3 proteins YWHAB, YWHAE and YWHAZ when phosphorylated on Ser-351. Interacts with the SH3 domain of ABL1 and ABL2. Interacts with RAB5A. The interaction with Ras is probably regulated and antagonized by the interaction with 14-3-3 proteins. The interaction with 14-3-3 proteins is regulated by phosphorylation on Ser-351"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"commentType": "INTERACTION", "interactions": [{"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q13671", "intActId": "EBI-366017"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P00519", "geneName": "ABL1", "intActId": "EBI-375543"}, "numberOfExperiments": 6, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q13671", "intActId": "EBI-366017"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P42684", "geneName": "ABL2", "intActId": "EBI-1102694"}, "numberOfExperiments": 7, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q13671", "intActId": "EBI-366017"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q49AR9", "geneName": "ANKS1A", "intActId": "EBI-11954519"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q13671", "intActId": "EBI-366017"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q7Z6G8-3", "geneName": "ANKS1B", "intActId": "EBI-17714371"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q13671", "intActId": "EBI-366017"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q13137", "geneName": "CALCOCO2", "intActId": "EBI-739580"}, "numberOfExperiments": 4, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q13671", "intActId": "EBI-366017"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q96L46", "geneName": "CAPNS2", "intActId": "EBI-12188723"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKB